[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605265100-fusion-fuel-sourcing-d-gate-evaluation-r0", :adr/title "Fusion fuel sourcing (D / T / Li-6 / He-3 / B-11) — D1..D5 evaluation R0 (sub-ADR of 2605263500 §2.3; supply-chain constraint analysis for the conditional-permit fusion R&D pathway)", :adr/status "proposed-pending-council-ratification", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605265100: Fusion fuel sourcing (D / T / Li-6 / He-3 / B-11) — D1..D5 evaluation R0\n\n**Status**: proposed-pending-council-ratification\n**Date**: 2026-05-26\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (Founder, Seat 1) — pending Council Lv7+ unanimity cascade\n\n# Context\n\nADR-2605263500 §2.3 (nuclear fusion conditional permit) establishes preference order aneutronic > D-D > D-T > D-He³ but defers sourcing-feasibility analysis. Each fuel has supply-chain constraints under D1 (no commercial-vendor / state-licensed-fuel-cycle dependency) and D4 (proliferation hygiene + dual-use caps). This ADR resolves the open question.\n\n| Fuel | Natural source | Religious-corp R&D scale need | Sourcing constraint |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Deuterium (²H)** | Seawater ~33 mg/L D₂O | ≤10 kg D / R3 facility | ✓ religious-corp electrolysis-distillation feasible |\n| **Tritium (³H)** | Bred from Li-6 + neutron OR commercial CANDU heavy-water | ≤10 kg religious-corp aggregate per §2.3.2 | ⚠ enrichment dual-use; CANDU commercial-state-licensed |\n| **Lithium-6 (⁶Li)** | Natural Li 7.5% Li-6, enriched to >20% for breeding | ≤100 kg religious-corp aggregate per §2.3.2 | ⚠ enrichment cascade dual-use (formerly Cold-War weapons-relevant) |\n| **Helium-3 (³He)** | Tritium decay OR lunar regolith OR cosmic-ray spallation | n/a — see §3 | ✗✗ EFFECTIVELY UNAVAILABLE |\n| **Boron-11 (¹¹B)** | Natural boron 80.1% B-11 + 19.9% B-10, B-10 depletion required for fusion | ≤500 kg religious-corp R3 | ✓ religious-corp mining + B-10 depletion via existing borax → boric acid → B-11-enriched-B₂O₃ chain feasible |\n\n# Decision\n\n## §1 Deuterium — SOURCING FEASIBLE per ADR-2605263500 §2.3.1 D-D preference\n\n| Gate | Assessment |\n|---|---|\n| **D1** | ✓ Seawater electrolysis at religious-corp scale (~33 mg D₂O / L seawater × 10^6 L = 33 kg D₂O = ~3.3 kg D; well within ≤10 kg need) |\n| **D2** | ✓ Heavy water D₂O is short-half-life chemical handling; not radioactive |\n| **D3** | ✓ Electrolysis can use hikari renewable electricity |\n| **D4** | ✓ Deuterium itself non-weaponizable as fuel; dual-use only via D-T fuel cycle |\n| **D5** | ✓ Girdler-sulfide process patents expired; modern bithermal exchange (Girdler-Sulfide) or electrolytic distillation are open-publication chemistry |\n\n**Conditions**:\n1. Sourcing: religious-corp seawater electrolysis on coastal LANDS-extended marine parcel (ADR-2605192330) OR mizuho R2+ desalination tail-stream concentration (D₂O enrichment factor ~5× as seawater goes from 33 mg/L to 165 mg/L tail)\n2. Open-publication process design Apache 2.0 + Rider per D5\n3. Inventory ≤10 kg D religious-corp aggregate per fusion R&D site\n4. Annual `silenDeuteriumInventoryReview` Council Lv6+ ≥3 (mass-balance, no third-party transfer)\n\n## §2 Tritium + Lithium-6 — CONSTRAINED per §2.3.2\n\n| Gate | Assessment |\n|---|---|\n| **D1** | ⚠ Tritium from commercial CANDU heavy-water is state-licensed-utility dependency (FAILED); Li-6-bred tritium requires religious-corp lithium-6 enrichment which is dual-use cascade technology |\n| **D2** | ✓ Tritium hazard half-life 12.3 yr (low-energy β); structural activation primary D2 concern, not tritium itself |\n| **D4** | ✗ Lithium-6 enrichment to >20% is historically weapons-relevant (Cold-War thermonuclear-secondary fuel); religious-corp enrichment capability acquisition is the binding D4 + §1.12 (Transparent Force open-source) constraint |\n\n**Conditions** (more restrictive than §1):\n\n1. **Commercial CANDU tritium PROHIBITED** — would require state-licensed utility supply contract (D1 + state-fuel-cycle dependency)\n2. **Lithium-6 enrichment capability acquisition Council Lv7+ unanimity** (CONSTITUTIONAL — same threshold as ADR-2605263500 D1..D5 framework amendment): the decision to develop / operate any Li-6 enrichment capability (laser AVLIS, plasma separation, ion-exchange COLEX, etc.) requires full Council Lv7+ unanimity per program; not Lv6+ ≥4/7 like §2.3.2 D-T program approval\n3. **Lithium-6 inventory cap ≤100 kg of >20%** per §2.3.2 inheritance (well below 10× safety factor relative to weapons-relevant kg-scale)\n4. **Tritium inventory cap ≤10 kg religious-corp aggregate** per §2.3.2 inheritance\n5. **Tritium handling protocols** open-publication Apache 2.0 + Rider per D5\n6. **Geographic isolation**: tritium-handling facility on LANDS parcel with: (a) ≥5 km buffer from non-religious-corp settlement, (b) jurisdictional regulatory regime compatibility per §2.3.8\n7. **D-T program activation Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 per program** per §2.3.2\n\n## §3 Helium-3 — EFFECTIVELY UNAVAILABLE; D-He³ fuel cycle DEFERRED indefinitely\n\nHe-3 sources:\n\n| Source | Religious-corp accessibility |\n|---|---|\n| Tritium decay (³T → ³He + e⁻ + ν̄ at 12.3 yr half-life) | Requires existing T inventory (§2.3.2 cap ≤10 kg → ≤0.6 kg ³He/yr equilibrium) — utterly inadequate for fusion-fuel scale |\n| Lunar regolith (~10 ppb in mare basalt; some 100+ kt extractable) | Requires lunar mining infrastructure — out of religious-corp scope through R5+ |\n| Cosmic-ray spallation in upper atmosphere | Trace amounts (~0.000137% of atmospheric helium) — kg-scale collection infeasible |\n| Commercial supply (US DoE Tritium Sustainment + Savannah River) | State-licensed, weapons-program-byproduct — D1 commercial-state dependency + D4 NPT-regime-adjacent supply chain |\n\n**Verdict**: D-He³ fuel cycle is **EFFECTIVELY UNAVAILABLE** through R5+ for religious-corp constitutional reasons (no D1-compliant sourcing). ADR-2605263500 §2.3.1 preference-order placement (D-He³ < D-D) is correct + this ADR makes the sourcing infeasibility explicit.\n\nRe-evaluation at R6+ ONLY if either: (a) religious-corp lunar-resource-access program emerges (out of scope for foreseeable R0-R5), OR (b) novel atmospheric / cosmic-ray-mediated collection technology emerges, OR (c) tritium-decay inventory accumulates beyond §2 cap which itself requires §2 amendment.\n\n## §4 Boron-11 — SOURCING FEASIBLE, ENABLES ANEUTRONIC p-B¹¹ FUSION PER §2.3.1 PREFERENCE\n\nNatural boron is 80.1% B-11 (the fusion-relevant isotope) + 19.9% B-10. For fusion fuel, B-10 should be depleted (B-10 has neutron capture cross-section that contaminates the aneutronic-purity advantage of p-B¹¹).\n\n| Gate | Assessment |\n|---|---|\n| **D1** | ✓ Borax (Na₂B₄O₇·10H₂O) mining is widespread (Turkey 73% global reserves, US 9%, Argentina 3%); religious-corp LANDS parcel siting in Turkey or US Southwest feasible; alternative = ex-mine-tailings reuse cross-actor with future religious-corp metallurgy (kanayama §3 of ADR-2605264600 precedent) |\n| **D2** | ✓ Boron compounds non-radioactive; B-10 depletion process produces enriched B-11 + depleted B-10 streams; neither is hazardous waste at fusion-fuel scale |\n| **D3** | ✓ No carbon in supply chain (mining + chemistry are CO₂-emitting but offset by hikari renewable energy per ADR-2605263500 §2.2 closed-loop) |\n| **D4** | ✓ Boron is non-fissile; B-10 has neutron-capture nuclear-medicine use but at fusion-fuel scale not proliferation-relevant |\n| **D5** | ✓ Open-publication thermal-diffusion column + chemical-exchange B-10/B-11 separation processes (post-WWII declassified) |\n\n**Conditions**:\n\n1. **B-10 depletion process open-hardware**: thermal-diffusion column or chemical-exchange (BF₃ + anisole, public-domain) per D5\n2. **Inventory ≤500 kg religious-corp R3** (corresponds to ~50 g B-10 byproduct depletion + ~450 g enriched B-11; well below proliferation concern — B-10 has Boron Neutron Capture Therapy medical use, dual-use scale starts at 100s of kg)\n3. **Sourcing per Charter §2(g) audit**: borate mineral supply audited for human-rights compliance (Turkish mining + US Southwest indigenous-land issues both flag for Council Lv6+ ≥3 per source)\n4. **Aneutronic p-B¹¹ fuel preparation**: proton-source = green H₂ via ADR-2605263600 §1 → H atoms (trivial); B-11 from §4.1 enriched powder; total fuel mass ≤1 kg/site/yr at R3 scale (proton-boron reaction is ~1000× lower cross-section than D-T, requires very high plasma density × confinement time)\n\n## §5 Fuel-cycle final ranking under sourcing analysis\n\n| Cycle | §2.3.1 a-priori rank | Sourcing | Final preference |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Aneutronic p-B¹¹ | 1st | ✓ ✓ | **1st (confirmed by §4)** |\n| D-D | 2nd | ✓ | **2nd (confirmed by §1)** |\n| D-T | 3rd | ⚠ §2 constraint | **3rd (operationally significantly more constrained than D-D due to §2 Council Lv7+ Li-6 enrichment gate)** |\n| D-He³ | 4th | ✗✗ | **EFFECTIVELY UNAVAILABLE (§3)** |\n\n**This ADR confirms ADR-2605263500 §2.3.1 fuel-cycle preference order via supply-chain feasibility analysis**: aneutronic p-B¹¹ is the only fully-religious-corp-sourceable fusion fuel at R&D scale; D-D is the second-most-accessible; D-T requires extraordinary Council Lv7+ unanimity per Li-6 enrichment capability acquisition; D-He³ is effectively unavailable.\n\n## §6 Roadmap\n\n| Phase | Scope | Cap |\n|---|---|---|\n| **R0** | This ADR (constitutional pre-evaluation only; no physical fuel handling) | None |\n| **R1** | post-Council ratification of 2605263500 + this ADR + first fusion R&D entry ADR (separate; per 2605263500 §P8 earliest ≥2027) + ≥1 nuclear-physicist + ≥1 isotope-chemist on Council | Bench-scale deuterium electrolytic distillation pilot (target ≤100 g D₂O); B-11 enrichment commercial-procurement evaluation Council Lv6+ ≥3 | 100 g D |\n| **R2** | post-R1 + 30-day public + cross-actor mizuho coastal-parcel attestation | ≤1 kg D religious-corp; first B-10 depletion process bench-scale ≤100 g B-11 | 1 kg D + 100 g B-11 |\n| **R3** | post-R2 + first religious-corp fusion R&D facility commissioning (separate ADR) | Full §1, §4 caps; §2 D-T only with separate Council Lv6+ ≥4/7 per-program + Council Lv7+ unanimity per Li-6 enrichment | per-fuel caps |\n\n## §7 New Lexicons (R1+)\n\n```\ncom.etzhayyim.hikari.{\n  fusionFuelInventoryAttestation,        # per-isotope: kg current + sourcing CID + Council attestation chain\n  deuteriumProductionAttestation,        # electrolysis source + D2O concentration + religious-corp attestation\n  boron11EnrichmentAttestation,          # enrichment process + B-10 depletion % + Charter §2(g) supply audit\n  tritiumInventoryAttestation,           # Li-6 → T breeding record OR (PROHIBITED) commercial source rejection\n  lithium6EnrichmentCapabilityAttestation, # Council Lv7+ unanimity record per program (constitutional)\n  silenFusionFuelSourcingReview          # annual Council Lv6+ ≥3 across all fusion-fuel pathways\n}\n```\n\n# Consequences\n\n**Positive**:\n- Resolves ADR-2605263500 §2.3.1 fuel-cycle preference-order ambiguity with supply-chain rigor\n- p-B¹¹ as primary fusion-fuel-target focuses religious-corp R&D on the only fully-self-sourceable pathway\n- B-11 enrichment capability has dual benefit: fusion fuel + Boron Neutron Capture Therapy medical isotope (cross-actor with iyashi R3+ clinical applications)\n- Li-6 enrichment capability acquisition Lv7+ unanimity gate makes D-T pathway operationally hard but possible — preserves option without committing\n\n**Negative**:\n- D-He³ unavailability rules out cleanest-aneutronic-with-He³ pathway; p-B¹¹ becomes the only aneutronic option (and p-B¹¹ has very challenging plasma physics)\n- B-10 depletion process is non-trivial chemistry + ~$100-500/kg natural B → enriched B-11; capex for ≤500 kg R3 ~$50-250K\n- Li-6 enrichment capability NEVER acquired (probably) means D-T fusion is operationally unavailable to religious-corp — limits R&D fuel-cycle choice to p-B¹¹ + D-D\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\n- **Permit commercial T procurement from CANDU utilities**: rejected (D1 + state-fuel-cycle dependency)\n- **Permit He-3 procurement from US DoE Savannah River**: rejected (D1 + weapons-program-byproduct supply chain)\n- **Skip aneutronic preference, focus on D-D**: considered — but §2.3.1 preference is established; aneutronic p-B¹¹ deserves R&D investment as the unique no-neutron-activation pathway\n- **Defer entire fusion-fuel-sourcing question until R4+ when actual fusion R&D ADR ratifies**: rejected — sourcing constraint is constitutional (D1 + D4) and properly belongs in pre-evaluation before R&D ADR commits resources\n\n# References\n\n- ADR-2605263500 §2.3 (parent fusion conditional permit)\n- ADR-2605263600 §1 (green H₂ as proton source for p-B¹¹)\n- ADR-2605192330 (extended LANDS for coastal D₂O sourcing)\n- ADR-2605192315 (Transparent Force open-source posture for §2 + §3)\n- ITER Open-Data Portal — fusion-fuel-cycle public reference\n- IAEA Lithium-6 enrichment public references (post-Cold-War declassified) — referenced for §2 dual-use baseline\n- US DOE Tritium Sustainment Program references — referenced as commercial path EXPLICITLY NOT USED per §2.1\n- Burnham, C. W. \"Boron isotope ratio measurements\" — natural B abundance reference\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605265100-fusion-fuel-sourcing-d-gate-evaluation-r0.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "fusion-fuel-sourcing-d-gate-evaluation", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-26", :adr/date "2026-05-26", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605192300-etzhayyim-bootstrap-council-five"], :adr/authoritative_for ["Fusion fuel sourcing feasibility per fuel cycle (D-D / D-T / D-He³ / p-B¹¹) under D1..D5" "Lithium-6 enrichment capability acquisition gate (Council Lv7+ unanimity)" "Helium-3 sourcing dependency analysis (lunar / fission-byproduct / cosmic-ray spallation)" "Boron-11 supply chain (natural-abundance enrichment OR religious-corp-mineable; aneutronic-fusion enabler)"]}]
